  {
    "case_id": "steam:229292137:2",
    "category": "universal_system_scope",
    "source": {
      "record_id": "steam:229292137",
      "platform": "steam",
      "source_id": "229292137",
      "text_original": "Its fun casually but the drive system is pretty flawed in terms of incentivizing fun gameplay. Drive Impact alone dominates low rank, and for how easy it is to use but how careful you need to be around it, it shouldn't give you the reward it does. I say this having abused it myself, its just boring and actually teaches some bad habits ive had to actively fight against. \r\n\r\nIn general the Drive system seems to conflict with SF's entire identity as a footsies fighter, or at the very least invalidates a lot of neutral gameplay.\r\n\r\nUnderneath the Drive hood, theres a fun game, and its not like it isnt fun generally. Capcom should be more attentive given how expensive the DLC is though, and hopefully a new version of the game releases that heavily tweaks, if not removes, the drive system. Akin to whats happened with GG STRIVE's Wild Assault move. But im a scrub ig so take this with a grain of salt idk.\r\n\r\nCapcom gets points for Elena at least, but wheres Makoto? lol",
      "language": "en",
